use std
into cloth_check.amni

Imports: os, math and gfx.cloth. A standalone program that checks the cloth solver on the CPU and prints one line per check. The solver's API, all in namespace `cloth`, with every number a `real`: `cloth::make(p, stride, at, nv, indices)` (p a read-only f32 slice, indices a read-only u32 slice, the rest int) builds a cloth and returns its number, an int; `cloth::pin(c int, vertex int, x real, y real, z real)` holds a mesh vertex at a point; `cloth::clear_colliders()`; `cloth::ball(x, y, z, r)` adds a sphere; `cloth::pill(ax, ay, az, bx, by, bz, r)` adds a capsule; `cloth::ground(y)` adds the floor; `cloth::step(c int, dt real, wx real, wy real, wz real)` advances by dt seconds in a wind; `cloth::write(c, p, stride, at, at_n, out)` (p a read-only f32 slice, out a writable f32 slice, the rest int) writes two morph targets, 16 floats per vertex; `cloth::stretch_now(c int) real`; `cloth::speed(c int) real`; `cloth::particle(c int, vertex int) int` is a vertex's particle. Module arrays of the solver that the checks read: `cloth::cloths` (records with int fields `p0`, the first particle, and `np`, the particle count, and the settings `substeps int` and `limit bool`, which a check may assign), `cloth::pos` and `cloth::nrm` (real, three per particle, particle i's values at index `i * 3`). `os` gives `clock_ns() int`. A step is always `1.0 / 60.0` seconds. Module vars: `P`, a growable f32 array (the sheet's vertices, six floats each: position then normal), `I`, a growable u32 array (its triangles), and `N`, an int (vertices along a side).

`fn sheet(n int, mode int)` fills `P` and `I` from scratch with a square sheet 1 m wide of n x n vertices and sets `N`. The vertex in row j, column i has index `j * n + i`; with `u = i / (n - 1) - 0.5` and `t = j / (n - 1)` as reals: mode 0 (hanging) puts it at `(u, 2 - t, 0)` with normal (0, 0, 1); mode 1 (flat) at `(u, 0.85, t - 0.5)` with normal (0, 1, 0); mode 2 (held out) at `(u, 2, t)` with normal (0, 1, 0). Every cell gives two triangles: with a the vertex (i, j) and b the vertex below it in row j + 1, they are (a, b, a + 1) and (a + 1, b, b + 1).

`fn fresh(n int, mode int, pins bool) int` clears the colliders, builds the sheet, makes a cloth from `P` with stride 6 and the position at offset 0, and when `pins` is true pins every vertex of row 0 at its own position. Returns the cloth.

`fn run(c int, steps int, wz real)` steps the cloth that many times with the wind (0, 0, wz).

`fn nearest(c int, ax real, ay real, az real, bx real, by real, bz real) real` is the smallest distance from any of the cloth's particles to the segment from a to b (to the point a when the two are equal).

`fn row_mean(c int, row int, axis int) real` is the mean of one coordinate (axis 0, 1 or 2) over the particles of the vertices in that row of the sheet; row -1 means every particle of the cloth.

`fn verdict(ok bool)` returns the text " PASS" or " FAIL" as a read-only byte slice.

`fn z1() bool`: a hanging pinned sheet of 33 after 180 steps has `stretch_now` s. The control is the same with the cloth's `substeps` set to 1 and `limit` set to false before stepping, giving sc. Passes when s is at most 1.03 and sc is above 1.03. Prints "cloth Z1 longest edge after 3 s ", s, " of rest (bar 1.03), control 1 substep without the pin limit ", sc, and the verdict.

`fn z2() bool`: a held-out pinned sheet of 33 stepped 600 times with no wind; `early` is `cloth::speed` after step 30 and `late` after the last. `finite` is true when every coordinate of every particle of the cloth equals itself and has an absolute value below 1e30. Passes when late is below 0.02, finite holds and early is above 0.02. Prints "cloth Z2 mean speed after 10 s ", late, " m/s (bar 0.02), finite ", finite, ", control at 0.5 s ", early, and the verdict.

`fn z3() bool` covers Z3 and Z7. A flat sheet of 33 without pins, with a sphere of radius 0.3 at (0, 0.5, 0) and the floor at 0, is stepped 180 times; `low` is the smallest value of `nearest` to the sphere's center seen after any step. At the end, `touch` counts particles whose distance d from the center has `abs(d - 0.304)` at most 0.002, and over the particles with `d - 0.305` at most 0.002, `ang` is the mean angle in degrees between the particle's normal in `cloth::nrm` and the direction from the center to the particle, while `flat_ang` is the same mean taking (0, 1, 0) as every normal. The control is the same sheet with the floor only: `clow` is its smallest `nearest` to (0, 0.5, 0) over the steps, and `lying` is true when at the end every particle's height is at least 0.004 and at most 0.02. Z3 passes when low is at least 0.304, touch is at least 100, clow is below 0.2 and lying holds; Z7 passes when ang is at most 15 and flat_ang is above 15. Prints "cloth Z3 nearest to the sphere's center ", low, " m (bar 0.304), touching at the end ", touch, " (bar 100), control without the sphere nearest ", clow, " lying on the ground ", lying, and Z3's verdict; then a second line "cloth Z7 normals against the sphere's ", ang, " degrees over the touching particles (bar 15), control rest normals ", flat_ang, and Z7's verdict. Returns true when both pass.

`fn z4() bool`: the same drop with a capsule of radius 0.1 from (-0.3, 0.5, 0) to (0.3, 0.5, 0) in place of the sphere, floor at 0, 180 steps; `low` is the smallest `nearest` to that segment after any step, and `clow` the same for a control without the capsule. Passes when low is at least 0.104 and clow is below 0.05. Prints "cloth Z4 nearest to the capsule's segment ", low, " m (bar 0.104), control without it ", clow, and the verdict.

`fn z5() bool`: a hanging pinned sheet of 33. For step k from 1 to 120: pin every vertex i of row 0 at `(i / (N - 1) - 0.5 + 0.5 * k / 60, 2, 0)` (as reals), step once with no wind, and let `off` keep the largest distance seen between a row 0 particle and the point it was just pinned at. `moved` is the bottom row's mean x at the end minus its mean x before the first step. The control is a hanging sheet without pins stepped 120 times; `drift` is the absolute change of the mean x over all its particles. Passes when off is at most 0.000001, moved is at least 0.8 and drift is below 0.01. Prints "cloth Z5 pins off their targets by at most ", off, " m (bar 0.000001), bottom row moved ", moved, " m (bar 0.8), control without pins moved ", drift, and the verdict.

`fn z6() bool`: a hanging pinned sheet of 33 stepped 180 times with wz 5 has bottom row mean z `blown`; the same with no wind has `calm`. Passes when blown is at least 0.2 and the absolute value of calm is at most 0.001. Prints "cloth Z6 bottom row in 5 m/s wind at z ", blown, " m (bar 0.2), control without wind ", calm, and the verdict.

`fn z10() bool`: a hanging pinned sheet of 65, and an f32 array `out` of `N * N * 16` zeros. 120 times: read the clock, step once with wz 5, call `cloth::write(c, P[..], 6, 0, 3, out[..])`, read the clock again and keep the difference in milliseconds. `med` is the median (sort ascending, element at index 60). Passes when med is at most 4. Prints "cloth Z10 one step of 4225 particles with the morph data ", med, " ms (bar 4, median of 120)", and the verdict.

`main()` runs z1, z2, z3, z4, z5, z6 and z10 in that order, all of them even after a failure, prints "cloth: ok" when all passed and otherwise "cloth: FAILED" and then exits with status 1.
